PODFoam llm_demo/hpc: the GPU path

These scripts run the asynchronous suite with Gemma 4 12B on a Slurm GPU
node. setup_12b.sh fetches the pinned weights and llama.cpp and checks
their SHA-256. build_llama_cuda.sh builds llama.cpp where the prebuilt
binaries need a newer glibc. start_server.sh and stop_server.sh check
that the pid they handle is a llama-server. async_v2.slurm runs the
suite with OpenFOAM in an Apptainer image; site settings come from the
environment. The runtime and the job records sit beside the repository.
Slurm's .out file goes to llm_demo/, which its .gitignore covers.

